// Core Real, a temporary axiomatic surface.
//
// Real is deliberately an ORDINARY omega::core declaration, not a compiler
// numeric primitive, standard-library convenience, or runtime float format.
// The opaque carrier has no layout.
// Its claim-free operations merely introduce proof symbols; each law is a
// separate accepted declaration and therefore a separate trust row. Replacing
// it with the constructive Cauchy quotient must keep the relation, witness,
// quotient and receiving-axiom contracts consumers rely on, not merely the
// names; PROOF-KERNEL-CORE on the board owns that work.

public boundary data Real;

public boundary machine Real::add(a: Real, b: Real) -> Real;
public boundary machine Real::multiply(a: Real, b: Real) -> Real;

boundary machine real_add_commutative(a: Real, b: Real)
ensures core::Identity<Real>(Real::add(a, b), Real::add(b, a));

boundary machine real_multiply_commutative(a: Real, b: Real)
ensures core::Identity<Real>(Real::multiply(a, b), Real::multiply(b, a));
